## ⚠️ CRITICAL — vitest root quirk

`pnpm test -w @platform/adapter-websocket` (and any `pnpm test` run from INSIDE
the package dir) prints **"No test files found"** — the root `vitest.config.ts`
include (`packages/*/src/**/*.test.ts`) is relative to the agentide root, but
vitest infers root from cwd. **The repo convention: run vitest from the agentide
ROOT**: `pnpm exec vitest run packages/adapter-websocket`, or root `pnpm test`
(all packages, `--passWithNoTests`). Same applies to backend-runtime — do NOT
"fix" package test scripts.

## Phase 2-9 roadmap (from IMPL, TDD red-green per phase)

1. **P2 `src/auth.ts`** — verifyToken (gateway-core), `originMatches`
   (**split at `*.` via indexOf — NEVER `.slice(1)`; the sim's slice bug ate the
   'h' of `https://`**; exact OR single-label right-anchored wildcard), pre-auth
   state machine (30s → close 1008; non-auth frames silently dropped),
   refresh = atomic claim swap carrying subs/in-flight/queue/connectionId,
   emits `event.connection.rotated` (internal, NOT relayed), no re-auth/prune
2. **P3 `src/registry.ts`** — ConnectionRegistry add/remove/get/snapshot/prune
3. **P4 `src/fanout.ts`** — per (conn × pattern) `eventBus.subscribe` with
   unsubscribe handle stored on record; **relay NEVER awaits socket.send**
   (bus dispatches with Promise.allSettled); `event.*` filtered (defense-in-
   depth — bus already blocks external publishes via RESERVED_INTERNAL_PREFIX);
   per-pattern authz at subscribe: `checkAuthz(scope, ["platform.<first>.read"])`
   (bare `*` → `platform.*.read`); batch all-or-nothing; dedupe idempotent;
   unsubscribe of never-subscribed → ok
4. **P5 `src/invoke.ts`** — invoke frame → `gateway.handleInvocation`; error
   PASSTHROUGH (no third vocabulary; e.g. GATEWAY_SESSION_NOT_FOUND passes
   verbatim on invoke.error); correlationId echo verbatim; stream mode wraps
   single-shot kernel call → `invoke.partial`×N + `invoke.end`; partials ride
   the same queue
5. **P6 `src/queue.ts`** — FIFO byte-budget queue, drop-OLDEST keep-newest while
   over `maxBufferedBytes`, cumulative `dropped`, stats frame ~1s after first
   drop (arm/disarm one-shot), drain via socket.send
6. **P7 `src/server.ts`** — `createWebSocketAdapter(gateway, eventBus, cfg)`;
   `ws.WebSocketServer` with **`maxPayload: maxFrameBytes` EXPLICITLY** (ws
   default is 100 MiB!); upgrade `req.headers.origin` captured on
   `connection(ws, req)`; heartbeat `socket.ping()` + `on('pong')` → close
   1011 (autoPong default true); outbound over-cap → error frame + 1009;
   `stop()` snapshot/unsubscribe/close/clear timers; `src/index.ts` re-exports
7. **P8 agentide wiring** — factory `adapterWs !== false` default ON, `wsPort`
   default 7300, start after gateway+backend-runtime, stop reverse, expose
   `platform.wsAdapter`, reuse bootstrapped secret; `types.ts` + `cli.ts`
   (opts out) + `index.ts` re-exports + `__tests__/websocket-adapter.test.ts`
8. **P9 post-impl sim** — `packages/agentide/scripts/simulate-websocket-adapter.mjs`
   (DIFFERENT script from simulate-pre.html; drive real adapter; PRD
   scenarios 1-14)

Then: `feature-pipeline-review` sub-agent, drift check (`drift read`), `update-backlog`,
git-flow commits (docs + code separately — root repo vs agentide repo).

## Locked contract in one screen (full detail: map.md / PRD-TRD / GRILL)

- Flat JSON-text envelope, **16 frame types**, no JSON-RPC, no version field v1
- Auth: JWT first message after open; `auth.ok {connectionId, claims}` |
  `auth.error {code, message}` + close **1008**; pre-auth timeout 30s;
  refresh = `auth` anytime, atomic, no re-auth, no prune
- Origin: per-token `expectedOrigins` claim (D-50 — mint side NOT built;
  adapter is ENFORCER only, browser clients stay denied until dashboard lands);
  Node (no Origin) bypass; mismatch → "origin mismatch" + 1008
- Subs: verbatim bus topics, `*` final segment only (validatePattern reuse),
  per-pattern authz `platform.<first>.read`, `event.*` reserved, no session
  scoping, no count cap, prune on close
- Pull: universal `invoke` (mode call|stream), `invoke.*` echo correlationId
- Backpressure: 1 MiB/conn, drop-oldest FIFO, `stats {dropped}` ~1/s cumulative
- Close codes: 1008 auth / 1011 heartbeat / 1009 frame too large

